  "verbalization": "Feigrisolide C is implicated in the interaction with Free fatty acid receptor 2 through multiple pathways, with varying levels of confidence. The evidence suggests that Feigrisolide C acts as a target for A172, which in turn targets Free fatty acid receptor 2. Similarly, other compounds such as 3-O-beta-D-glucopyranosyl-oleanolic acid 28 O-beta-D-glucopyranoside and (3R,4R)-3-(1,3-benzodioxol-5-ylmethyl)-4-[(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)methyl]oxolan-2-one also share the same target relationship. These findings collectively indicate that Feigrisolide C may exert its biological effects through a network of compounds that ultimately engage Free fatty acid receptor 2. The mechanisms underlying this interaction likely involve the activation of receptor signaling pathways, which are commonly associated with cellular responses to fatty acids. The strength of the evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a potential role for Feigrisolide C in modulating receptor activity. However, the exact molecular mechanisms and the precise nature of the interactions remain areas of further investigation."
